# Everything that must not reach the build context. Two reasons, and the second
# is the one that bites: a large context is slow, but a context containing .env
# or .git bakes credentials and history into a layer that ships.

.git
.github

# Local configuration. .env holds real credentials; .env.example is committed
# and carries only placeholders, but neither is read at build time.
.env
**/.env

# Build output and coverage artefacts from the host. Copying a darwin binary
# into a linux image produces an exec format error at the least useful moment.
bin/
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Nothing below is compiled into the binary. migrations/ is deliberately absent
# from this list: it is not linked into the api or the worker, but the migrate
# stage copies it, and the build context is shared by all three targets.
docs/
prompts/
test/
api/bruno/
deployments/
README.md
README.zh-CN.md
STATE.md
LICENSE
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
.golangci.yml
sqlc.yaml

**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
**/__pycache__/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
